PART 4: VPC (Virtual Private Cloud)

Interview importance: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ (Highest Priority)

VPC is one of the most important AWS services for DevOps and Cloud Infrastructure roles. Many interviews spend 20–40 minutes on networking concepts because they directly affect application availability and security.

What is a VPC?

A Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) is a logically isolated virtual network within AWS where you launch and manage AWS resources.

Think of it as your own private data centre in the cloud.

Without a VPC:

AWS Cloud
    |
Everyone shares same network

With a VPC:

AWS Cloud
      |
-------------------------
|       Your VPC        |
|                       |
|  EC2   RDS   Lambda   |
|                       |
-------------------------
Why Do We Need a VPC?

A VPC provides:

Network isolation
IP address management
Security
Internet connectivity
Private communication
Routing control

Without a VPC, you wouldn't control:

IP addresses
Firewall rules
Subnets
Routes
Internet access
